# Fleet optimization W4a: a hung seat and a provider limit are detected, held or retried, and reported. Issues 92 and 84. Tier C, at most two critic rounds, targeted tests. 2026-09-14
#
# DISPATCH: ./scripts/dispatch.sh git@github.com:Arlencho/dev-agents.git wave-plans/dev-agents/2026-09-14-w4a-seat-reliability.plan --detach --retries 1
# AFTER: wave-plans/dev-agents/2026-09-14-w2-risk-tiers.plan
# TIER: C
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1 | web-frontend | Branch feat/w4a-seat-reliability from origin/main after the W2 PR has merged. Read issues 92 and 84 first; they carry the observed signatures. ONE, issue 92: run-remote tracks the time of the last model event per seat (an assistant or tool result event, never a heartbeat or thinking-token tick); after a quiet period, default 30 minutes, configurable, the seat is stopped with a distinct exit code, dispatch.sh retries it once, and a stop row names the seat and the quiet period. TWO, issue 84: the launcher recognises a provider limit exit (seat under 15 seconds, no API time, is_error true, result text naming a spend or session limit, or the existing 401 pattern) and returns a distinct exit code; dispatch.sh does not burn the retry on it, marks the seat held, not failed, and writes a stop row with the provider and the reset time from the message; no further seat on that provider and model starts until a probe call succeeds. Tests with fixtures copied from the real logs of 2026-09-13 and 2026-09-14 named in the issues: a quiet seat is stopped and retried once; a heartbeat-only seat counts as quiet; a limit exit is held with the reset time; the retry is not consumed; a probe success releases the hold. VERIFY: the test file you add plus tests/run-worktree-tests.sh only, real exit codes in the PR body; no full suite. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Open a draft PR titled Fleet optimization W4a: hung seats and provider limits, Closes 92, Closes 84. | feat/w4a-seat-reliability

2 | plan-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the PR on branch feat/w4a-seat-reliability. Tier C, round 1 of at most 2. No commits, no push, no review, no labels; tmp writes only. Record head SHA at start and at report. THE QUESTION THAT MATTERS: can a working seat be killed, or a dead seat stay unnoticed. Try a long silent tool run that still emits tool results, a heartbeat-only seat, a limit message worded differently, two seats on the same provider at the limit. Report only findings that kill working seats or leave dead seats running. Post ONE comment on the PR whose first line reads CRITIC W4A SEAT RELIABILITY with SAFE-TO-MERGE, BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE and citations. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash, no AI tool or vendor name. | feat/w4a-seat-reliability
